.TH CODEXFLARE 1 "2026-11-01" "Codexflare 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codexflare \- edit Codex startup animation and workspace background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codexflare
.RI [ --port " PORT" ]
.RI [ --headless ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a native GTK/WebKit editor for local videos, PNG backgrounds,
playback parameters, and startup window settings.
Saving settings does not apply them to Codex.
Quit Codex normally before applying settings in the editor.
.PP
Patching checks the resources and window structures of Linux x86_64 Codex
installed in /usr/lib/chatgpt. Unrecognized structures are rejected;
preview and save remain available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --port PORT
Choose the loopback HTTP port. The default selects an available port.
.TP
.B --headless
Run only the local test server without opening a desktop window.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.SH FILES
User settings, imported media, backups, and the patched runtime are kept
under $XDG_DATA_HOME/codexflare, defaulting to ~/.local/share/codexflare.
The system Codex installation and account data are not modified.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR codexflare-manage (1)
.PP
https://github.com/epsilon10111/Codexflare
